
## tree.aside · --help
rc=0
git.tree.aside — set a tree's uncommitted edits aside under a tag, then lay them back

usage:
  rhx git.tree.aside set --tag <tag> --path <file> [--path <file> …]
  rhx git.tree.aside get --tag <tag>
  rhx git.tree.aside get                 # every entry held

## tree.aside · bare get, none held
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get
   └─ (none held)

## tree.aside · set feat.old (a.txt)
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside set --tag feat.old
   ├─ sha: <sha>
   └─ paths
      └─ a.txt

## tree.aside · set feat (b.txt)
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside set --tag feat
   ├─ sha: <sha>
   └─ paths
      └─ b.txt

## tree.aside · a held tag refuses
rc=2
🐢 lets set it aside...

✋ ConstraintError: tag 'feat' is already held
   └─ lay it back first: rhx git.tree.aside get --tag feat

## tree.aside · bare get lists both
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get
   ├─ feat (<sha>)
   ├─ feat.old (<sha>)

## tree.aside · an absent tag refuses
rc=2
🐢 lets set it aside...

✋ ConstraintError: no entry holds tag 'nope'
   └─ see what is held: rhx git.tree.aside get

## tree.aside · bare get lists no foreign entry
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get
   ├─ feat (<sha>)
   ├─ feat.old (<sha>)

## tree.aside · get feat lays feat alone
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get --tag feat
   ├─ sha: <sha>
   └─ laid back, entry dropped

## tree.aside · get feat.old lays it
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get --tag feat.old
   ├─ sha: <sha>
   └─ laid back, entry dropped

## tree.aside · set moved (a.txt)
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside set --tag moved
   ├─ sha: <sha>
   └─ paths
      └─ a.txt

## tree.aside · a moved path refuses, entry kept
rc=2
🐢 lets set it aside...

✋ ConstraintError: HEAD moved 1 held path(s) since 'moved' was set
   ├─ a.txt
   ├─ the entry is KEPT, and no file was touched
   └─ read what it holds: git stash show -p <sha>

## tree.aside · the kept entry still lists
rc=0
🐢 lets set it aside...

🐚 git.tree.aside get
   ├─ moved (<sha>)

## exec.set · --help
rc=0
file.exec.set — give a file inside this repo its exec bit

usage:
  rhx file.exec.set --path <file> [--path <file> …]

it refuses a path outside this repo, a dir, or a symlink

## exec.set · a file gains its bit
rc=0
🐢 lets make it runnable...

🐚 file.exec.set
   └─ + run.sh

## exec.set · a second run reports, writes naught
rc=0
🐢 lets make it runnable...

🐚 file.exec.set
   └─ = run.sh (already runnable)

## exec.set · a path outside the repo refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: <home>/.bash_aliases is outside this repo (<repo>)

## exec.set · a dir refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: dir is no regular file

## exec.set · a symlink refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: link.sh is a symlink; name the file it points at

## exec.set · no --path refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: name at least one --path

## reset.probe · --help
rc=0
######################################################################
# .what = run the usage-reset reader on one usage node, and show what jq said
#
# .why  = `_brains_auth_reset_line` sinks jq's stderr and prints
#         `? could not read the reset fields` on any failure, so a jq that
#         cannot parse the program reads the same as a node that lacks the
#         fields. this names which, with the jq version beside it
#
# usage:
#   rhx brains.auth.reset.probe                      # the cli's real-offer shape
#   rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --node '<json>' [--kind full|fable]
#   rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --from checkout      # read this checkout's copy, not ~/
#
# guarantee:
#   - READ-ONLY: no network, no account read; it runs the reader on the node given
######################################################################

## reset.probe · the default node
rc=0
🔬 brains.auth.reset.probe --kind full --from checkout
   ├─ jq: <jq>
   ├─ reader: 🎁 session reset available now
   └─ jq stderr: (none) ✔

## reset.probe · an unknown arg refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: unknown arg: --bogus
   fix: rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --help

## reset.probe · no installed reader refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: no reader at <home>/.bash_aliases.brains.auth.sh

## grove.sync · --help
rc=0
git grove sync — register each new hetzner grove the tailnet holds; never deletes
   usage: git grove sync [--mode plan|apply]   # plan is the default

## grove.sync · an unknown arg refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: unknown arg '--bogus'
   usage: git grove sync [--mode plan|apply]

## grove.sync · a --mode outside plan|apply refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --mode is plan or apply, got 'go'

## reach.set · a --gitroot that is no repo refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --gitroot '<home>/notrepo' is not a git repo
   fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.12.rack --mode apply   (it owns the rack root)

## reach.del · a --gitroot that is no repo refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --gitroot '<home>/notrepo' is not a git repo
   fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.12.rack --mode apply   (it owns the rack root)

